## Keep walking

Walk every day if you can, building up the distance over time. Walk until the pain gets quite bad, rest until it goes, then carry on.

## Look after your feet

Poor blood flow means cuts and sores heal slowly and can become infected.

- check your feet every day for cuts, sores or colour changes
- wear comfortable shoes and keep your feet warm
- see a **podiatrist** for nail and foot care, especially if you have diabetes
- get help quickly for any sore that is not healing

## Heart healthy living

- stop smoking
- eat less saturated fat and salt
- keep diabetes, blood pressure and cholesterol under control

## Support

The **Circulation Foundation** has information about PAD and its treatment.
